# Authentication & Authorization (Spring Security)

## Dependencies

- spring-boot-starter-security; jjwt (or nimbus-jose-jwt) for JWT parse/generate.

## Configuration

- @EnableWebSecurity; @EnableMethodSecurity for @PreAuthorize.
- SecurityFilterChain: permitAll for public paths (login, health); authenticate for API; JWT filter before UsernamePasswordAuthenticationFilter; sessionManagement stateless for API.
- JWT filter: extract Bearer token; validate (signature, expiry, issuer/audience); build Authentication (e.g. JwtAuthenticationToken) and set SecurityContextHolder.

## Method Security

- @PreAuthorize("hasRole('ADMIN')"), @PreAuthorize("hasAuthority('read:resource')"); use for controller or service methods.
- For resource-level: check in service (e.g. userId matches resource owner) and throw AccessDeniedException or return 403.

## Conventions

- JWT in Authorization header; short-lived access token; validate on every request; roles/authorities from token or DB; never log tokens.

## Anti-Patterns

- Storing sensitive data in JWT; no expiry; missing method security on protected endpoints; trusting client for resource ownership

